ars the labour party you know we've  discussed are  in an existential crisis this should be  a golden opportunity for you guys  shouldn't it and yet here you are just  making a couple of games here and there  you know taking  the odd council to no overall control i  mean it  shouldn't you be setting your sights a  bit higher than this well do we want to  make even more progress of course we do  but this is solid progress i mean the  seven gains in wiltshire was a really  highlight the five games in  cambridgeshire we took as you say power  away from the conservatives  these are areas of our strengths and you  know i go back to  key areas where we have real prospects  to beat conservative mps in the next  election places like cheadle and hazel  grove like guilford  um you know these are places where we  made real progress  and so uh if you're thinking about next  general election which uh indeed sky was  doing i mean  uh your own political reporter sam coats  when he was showing that we won 70  percent of the vote  he was making the point this liberal  democrats eating into the conservative  vote  and in your own projections you don't  see the greens winning any seats  you see labour winning a few seats you  see liberal democrats winning more seats  against the conservatives  because you do very well usually in  local elections normally a lot better  than this  well i mean we are very strong in local  government you're right we've got over  two and a half thousand councils across  the country  and local government is very important  to what liberal democrats are about  but we have to rebuild that base as we  did on thursday night  so that we can then translate that into  victors against the conservatives of the  next general election  so you know i i think in that frame in  that mission that we've set ourselves  we made real progress how concerned are  you by the green party  i know you say that the projection shows  they wouldn't win seats but at the same  time they